## Licensing (audit 2026-10-26)
Clean room and permissive-only (CLAUDE.local.md, CLA.md:95-100). Ranked; 1, 2 and 4 break the rules, the rest are missing notices.
- [x] 1. Threshold methods from GPL/unclear code: `threshold.rs:523` "All ported from ImageJ's AutoThresholder Java source", Otsu "diffed directly against the real source" - that file is Landini's Auto_Threshold (GPL in Fiji, parts from Celebi's Fourier library), not ImageJ 1's own public-domain code. ~15 functions (`thresh_otsu`, `_li`, `_min_error`, `_triangle`, `_moments`, `_huang`, `_intermodes`, `_isodata`, `_max_entropy`, `_mean`, `_minimum`, `_percentile`, `_renyi_entropy`, `_shanbhag`, `_yen`, lines ~551-1300). Rewrite from the papers (Otsu 1979, Li & Tam 1998, Kittler & Illingworth 1986, Zack 1977, Tsai 1985, Huang & Wang 1995, Prewitt & Mendelsohn 1966, Ridler & Calvard 1978, Kapur 1985, Glasbey 1993, Doyle 1962, Shanbhag 1994, Yen 1995) or port scikit-image's (BSD-3, with its notice). ImageJ as a black box for reference values is fine. Drop the "faithful port"/"literal translation" wording (also the tests' comments at ~1927, ~2030) and the out-of-tree literal translation. - done 2026-10-26: all 15 rewritten from the papers (clean room: old bodies never read, removed by script), each cites its paper (new `LI_TAM`, `SAHOO_RENYI`; DOIs checked on Crossref). Changed bins: Li 84 → 83, MinError 80 → 81, Triangle 42 → 41 (pipeline test 658 → 660 px), IsoData/Percentile/Moments/Renyi/Intermodes/Minimum differ on some histograms (see threshold.rs tests); Li/MinError/IsoData/MaxEntropy/Renyi 3-40× faster. To check against the papers: Shanbhag membership functions, Renyi β weights, Huang (PDF unreadable).
- [x] 2. YOLOv5 post-processing matched to Ultralytics' code (AGPL): `crates/ai/src/torch/yolov5.rs:192, 257, 331` (`non_max_suppression`, `process_mask(upsample=True)`, gray 114, `max_det`), reference from an out-of-tree `make_reference.py` that "re-implemented" them (`crates/core/src/algos/ai_segmentation/yolov5.rs:558-560`). If written from Ultralytics' source: rewrite from YOLACT (Bolya 2019) + standard NMS (torchvision's is BSD-3); check `make_reference.py` has no Ultralytics code; reword comments to the model's output format. - done 2026-10-26: written from the output format (owner), now restructured after YOLACT (Bolya 2019, cited) + greedy per-class NMS; `make_reference.py` remark removed. Identical output on synthetic windows; masks only around each box: 300 boxes 410-785 → 1.3-7.9 ms/window, peak ~870 → ~120 MB. Real-model test not run (`tests/university_of_sbg_brightfield_cell_segmentation_v3/` missing).
- [x] 3. Ports from permissive code without their notice (BSD/MIT need the copyright, conditions and disclaimer in the source and with the binary): `cellpose.rs:233-602` (`masks_to_flows` "kept faithful (including its quirks)", `steps_interp`, `get_masks_torch`, `remove_bad_flow_masks`, `steps2D`; Cellpose BSD-3, © HHMI), `feature_transform.rs` (SciPy `ni_morphology.c`, BSD-3), `propagation.rs` + `image_quality.rs` (centrosome/CellProfiler BSD-3, names the license only), `texture.rs` (mahotas MIT, if code was translated), `shape.rs` (scikit-image/centrosome BSD-3, if code was translated). One `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES` with the full texts, shown in the About dialog and shipped with every release; README.md:410 lists the ported projects. - done 2026-10-26: full texts in crates/gui/src/third_party_notices.json (About > Licenses), a license line in cellpose.rs, feature_transform.rs, propagation.rs, image_quality.rs, texture.rs; shape.rs left without (own code to scikit-image's definitions, not translated); shipping the texts in release archives stays with 5.
