## Algorithms
- [x] Add measure distance command - Measure Object Distance To Parent (centre and minimum distance to the parent) and Measure Object Neighbors (first/second closest distance), 2026-10-24
- [x] **A classifier with empty input classes brings "removed" objects back** - fixed 2026-10-26: in both classifiers neither input classes nor a segmentation class = the step does nothing, with a warning at the step (`module_checks`); both given = an object must match both; a segmentation class alone still selects class-less objects - on purpose, the way to bring removed objects back. "Add to pipeline" after training gives the AI step the classes the enabled pipelines give objects (`classes_the_pipelines_give`). (User report 2026-10-20): "Object classifier (remove small objects) -> AI object classifier" has the small objects in the results again; the other order works. A removed object only loses its classes and stays in `object_cache`; empty input classes select every visible object, class-less ones too (`matches_input` in `ai_object_classifier.rs`, the same filter in `classify_objects.rs`), and "Reclassify on match" / "Add class" gives them a class again. Same with a second Object classifier. Workaround: set the input classes. Fix (decide - changes the documented "regardless of its current class"): (A, preferred) empty input classes = all objects that still have a class, in both classifiers; or (B) drop objects from the cache when their last class goes. Check first whether a step or export uses class-less objects on purpose.
