## AI training panel (2026-10-24, design canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/894XNBXGBhmS1VeqYoPwfk, proposal 2)

- [x] Panel on the right as before (440 px sheet), no wizard: classifier switch + one-line explanation, classes with live example counts, "Examples from" summary, features (pixel: channel chips, presets Simple/Recommended/All, a table of what it sees × size 1/2/4/8/16 px + "+ size", options per row; object: shape checkboxes, brightness statistic × channel table, presets), Model and Training options folded to one-line summaries, example objects folded (class per object, exclude from training), fixed footer: readiness hint (can't yet / weak / ready - Train off until 2 classes have examples), name, Load…, Train. Rendered offscreen and checked; generated Slint code 56.91 → 56.73 MB.
- [x] Refreshes while open (objects drawn, classes changed, channels arriving), keeping what the user ticked (`AiLearningState.project_changed`).
- [x] Pixel classifier on several image channels: `AiLearningPixelFeatureSettings::image_channels` (empty: the image the step gets, as before); training reads them all; the step takes them from the tile's channel cache. Feature order: image channel × recipe entry. Size s px = Gaussian sigma s/2 (Gaussian blur limits raised to sigma 8, kernel 49); rank filter radius s.
- [x] Look at the panel in the real app (draw while open, train a pixel and an object classifier on 2 channels, load a model back). - checked in the real app (2026-10-26)
- [x] Preview of a trained model (decided 2026-10-24): through the user's own pipeline - the AI classifier step with the model; retraining under the same name overwrites the file (the classifier cache reloads a changed file), and a saved model triggers the auto preview (`UiState::model_saved`). The result says when no step uses the model yet. No temporary pipeline.
- [ ] Result card with accuracy per class: training reports trees/samples or losses only - the held-back examples' accuracy (overall, per class, which classes get mixed up) needs computing in training (`fit_classifier`).
- [ ] Training options hidden (2026-10-26, user finding): "Balance classes", "Normalize features" and "Hold back" were in the dialog but never passed to training (`balance_classes`, `normalize_features`, `validation_split` exist in Slint only). The section is removed from `ai_learning_dialog.slint`, the fields stay. To bring it back: Normalize = z-score per feature, stored in the model so prediction uses the same (matters for KNN / MLP - their features have very different scales; Random Forest doesn't need it); Balance = class weights or oversampling; Hold back = a held-back split and the result card above.
- [x] "Add to pipeline" after training (2026-10-24): offered when no step applies the model yet; adds a pipeline "AI · ‹model›" (`pipeline_for_model`): pixel - classifier → connected components → extract objects on the first trained channel, every trained class mapped to itself (objects in the class colours); object - the AI object classifier alone, no image of its own, last (adds the predicted class). One undo step; the pipelines panel lists and selects it (`UiState::pipeline_added`), the auto preview runs it.
- [ ] Models from the old dialog whose features aren't table cells load their settings but keep the table (logged).
- [x] Feature rows under their real names (Raw image, Gaussian blur, Gaussian gradient (Sobel), Laplacian / Hessian of Gaussian, Structure tensor, Rank filter); the raw image its own row; size columns share the table width (header and checkboxes line up), a click on a size removes it, at most 10; the brightness table's columns adapt to the channels (numbers + legend when narrow, scrolls sideways beyond ~10); the object preset is remembered (was: "Recommended" looked dead before the channels were known) - 2026-10-24.
- [x] The model stores its channels' names (`image_channel_names`, for information); channels are found by their number - matching by name was built and removed again (decided 2026-10-24: too many edge cases, images without names; keeps the job executor simple). No mapping UI.
- [ ] Check before an analysis that the images have the model's channels (today: an error per image during the run); report training images skipped for a missing channel.
- [x] Object classifier training measures on demand (2026-10-24), like pixel training: `ObjectTrainingJob` gets the labeled objects per image (`TrainingImage`) and measures each one's intensities from the file (own z/t plane, all channels, full resolution, only the regions with objects - `object::regions::measure_on_planes`, shared with the app's annotation measuring). Shape features alone open no image. The stored annotation intensities aren't used for training any more; the "spread not measured" skip is gone; an unreadable image → `ImageFailed`, its objects skipped.
- [x] Ring features (2026-10-24): "Ring mean" and "Contrast to ring" (object mean − ring mean) rows in the brightness table, ring width (default 5 px) under it while one is ticked, stored in the model (`AiLearningObjectFeatureSettings::ring_width`). Ring = every pixel ≤ width px from the object (Euclidean), minus the object, neighbours included, cut to the image (`ring_mask`). Made on demand in training and in the AI Object Classifier step (measured from the channel cache like the objects); test `training_and_the_pipeline_step_compute_the_same_features` (identical values). Not in "Recommended".
- [x] "Minimum certainty" in the AI Pixel Classifier step (2026-10-24, default 0 = off): pixels below it become background. Certainty = share of trees voting for the class (random forest; trees read once through serde, smartcore keeps them private), share of neighbours (KNN `predict_proba`), softmax probability (MLP).

## AI plugin

Done 2026-10-19: libtorch is loaded only on the first AI step, from a plugin library next to the program (`ai/cpu`, `ai/cuda`). The app no longer links libtorch.

- One crate, `crates/ai` (`evanalyzer_ai`), one module per part:
  - `api` - engine-neutral: `Request`/`Task` (one variant per model kind), `Response`, `EngineConfig`, the `InferenceEngine` trait, the C interface (`eva_ai_api_version`, `eva_ai_init`, `eva_ai_infer`, `eva_ai_free`; postcard bytes, image by pointer).
  - `torch` (feature `torch`, the only code with `tch`): scheduler (device slots, per-device model cache, OOM retry), the four models' tensor code, the C exports (`catch_unwind`, log forwarding).
  - `runtime` - plugin loader (feature `torch-plugin`) and CUDA driver probe; the crate root picks the engine once: `torch` linked in (tests) > the plugin > "no AI model support". Plugin search: `EVANALYZER_AI_PLUGIN`, next to the program, `ai/cuda` (driver sees a GPU, CPU not asked for), `ai/cpu`, then `ai/cuda` (CUDA libtorch on the CPU). CUDA probe through the NVIDIA driver (`cuInit` + `cuDeviceGetCount`), not libtorch.
  - The plugin = this crate as a cdylib with `torch`: `cargo build-ai-plugin` (`cargo rustc --crate-type cdylib`; no cdylib in the manifest, or every build depending on the crate would link a torch-less copy).
- Features: core/app/bin `libtorch` (bin default); the old `ai` feature is gone - trained classifiers (Burn, smartcore) are always built.
- Another engine (e.g. Burn once the models are converted) = a module with an `InferenceEngine` and one arm in `start` (crates/ai/src/lib.rs); the model steps only build `Request`s.

Open:
- [x] Smoke test the packages on real machines: "no plugin", "CPU plugin", "CUDA plugin without GPU", "CUDA plugin with GPU" - Linux, Windows (DLL search flags), macOS (install names, ad-hoc signing of `ai/cpu`). - works on real machines (2026-10-26)
- [x] **No more `torch_cuda` relink** (2026-10-19): the app loads `libtorch_cuda.so` / `torch_cuda.dll` from the plugin's folder right after the plugin, before its first libtorch call (it registers CUDA when loaded; the CPU build has none) - `crates/ai/build.rs` is gone, the release checks now check that the CUDA library is packaged in `ai/cuda`. Test: `the_cuda_library_next_to_the_plugin_is_loaded_with_it`. Still to confirm on a GPU machine (smoke test above): CUDA available, engine "libtorch (CUDA)". Note: with libtorch linked into a test binary (`torch` feature) CUDA is no longer registered there - those tests run on the CPU.
- [ ] The Windows plugin build (`cargo xwin rustc … --crate-type cdylib`) has not run yet - first release CI run.
- [ ] **Windows CUDA: "Cannot load symbol cudnnGetVersion"** (user report 2026-10-19, Cellpose-SAM) - fixed, not yet confirmed: libtorch loads cuDNN / nvrtc only at the first inference, with the process' DLL search, which didn't include `ai\cuda`. The plugin folder is now added for every later load (`SetDllDirectoryW` + `AddDllDirectory`, `search_later_loads_in` in crates/ai/src/runtime/plugin.rs). Linux is safe by construction (libtorch_cuda NEEDs libcudnn; every cudnn lib has RUNPATH $ORIGIN); macOS has no CUDA.
- [x] **No second libtorch** (2026-10-19): only a plugin that fails to *load* lets the next one be tried; one that loads but fails to set up is set up again for the CPU (CUDA libtorch runs there too), else it is the error - its library is kept (leaked), never closed.
- Once loaded, libtorch can't be unloaded; a libtorch crash still takes down the app (no process isolation).
- Maybe later: one plugin build for both variants (only the shipped libtorch differs). Untested.

## UI component library

Done with the Ink redesign (2026-10-17): the old `components/` folder is gone - every dialog uses `InkDialog` (About is custom on purpose), buttons, fields, chips, menus, rows, settings rows, tabs and dividers come from `crates/gui/ui/ink/`. This round: `InkFact` (object card + objects panel), plain dividers → `InkDivider`, the AI dialog's private header/divider → `InkCaption`/`InkDivider`, dead `CategoryChip` removed (generated code −12 KB).

Kept private on purpose (one screen's own, not a copy of an Ink piece): the step picker's category header and filter chips (category colours), pipeline step / parameter rows, the plate's wells, About's cards. `FormLabel` (AI training, module dialogs) stays a plain `Text` in Ink's style: `InkLabel`'s elide costs ~2 KB per use, 35 uses.

- [ ] Lower priority: `std-widgets` `ScrollView` (14×) / `ListView` (6×) / `TextEdit` (2×) are still Slint's own - an Ink scroll bar would make scrolling look the same everywhere.


