  - [x] `measurements.related_object_id UUID` (`ObjectValue { object, value, related }`); in the "one row per value" export after `object_id`. Not shown in the results yet - with step 4.
  - [x] Object measurements also on the object: `objects.measurement_values DOUBLE[]` at `measurement_info.object_index` - the results read them without a join (10 measurement columns per image 2.1 s / 4.2 GB → 77 ms / 285 MB on 5.6M objects; +109 MB file for 10 values per object). `measurements` stays for SQL and the long export.
  - [x] Results: plain per-object number columns read with `column_aggregate_expr` in the list too (`is_value_column`, `ObjectRow::values`) - new columns need a key/label and an expression, no `ObjectRow` field.
