- [x] 2. Object intensity spread (2026-10-24): std, median, lower/upper quartile, MAD per channel, CellProfiler's numbers exactly (fixture `crates/core/tests/object_intensity.json`: 57 objects through the accumulator and Extract Objects). `objects.intensity_{std,median,lower_quartile,upper_quartile,mad}_gray DOUBLE[]`; all intensity lists in gray values only - the `_normalized` ones are gone (nothing read them; writing -8 %, file -26 %, -0.6 GB RAM for 3.8M objects × 6 channels); `Column::IntensityStd/Median/LowerQuartile/UpperQuartile/Mad(channel)` (keys `intensity_<name>_gray_ch<n>`); CSV storage the same. Tile merge measures a merged object again from every tile it covers (all values - the additive merge of sum/min/max is gone; channels missing while the fragments had intensities is an error). Stored annotations: `distribution: None` → NULL. `Intensity::pixel_values` / `IntensitySettings::pixel_values` removed.
  - Cost (BENCHMARK.md): `bench_pipeline` median 5.57 → 6.62 s (big objects, 507M pixels), +50 MB; writing 3.8M objects × 6 channels +13 %, file +50 %. Order statistics by a 65535-level histogram (exact for 8/16-bit, else selection, small objects sorted).
